    rationale:
      "It re-surfaced leads-client-pending-announcement-deferred-needs-rtl-infra: of roughly 64 dashboard action buttons on /dashboard/leads gated on one shared `isPending` from a single `useTransition()`, only 3 change their visible label while pending; the other ~61 give a screen-reader or keyboard-only operator zero feedback that a click registered until the action resolves. That entry deliberately deferred a fix rather than shipping a cosmetic no-op, reasoning that (a) most of those buttons' accessible name comes from a *static* dashboardRowActionAriaLabel(...) call that never varies with isPending, so a per-button label ternary would change sighted-only visible text while the announced name stays frozen, and (b) the component's own documented focus-loss-on-disable race (dashboard-focus-restore-async-transition-race) means a button's label at the instant it disables isn't reliably what focus/announcement would pick up anyway. It named the actually-correct fix as 'a single shared aria-live operation-in-progress announcement decoupled from any individual button's disabled/focus state' and left two prerequisites for whoever picked this back up: decide on jsdom/@testing-library/react render-test infra vs. an explicit git-stash-exemption carve-out for pure-JSX changes, and design the fix as that shared region rather than per-button edits.\n\nResolved prerequisite one without adding new test infrastructure: this is a new-capability addition, not a behavioral bug fix (nothing was ever announced before, so there is no prior behavior to regress to), which AGENT_PROTOCOL already treats as exempt from the git-stash regression technique - verified instead via new unit tests on the underlying pure logic plus a dev-server smoke check of the rendered UI, exactly the carve-out the deferred entry anticipated. Confirmed via `grep -i testing-library package.json` (no match) that no render-test infra has been added since - the deferred entry's assessment still holds, and this fix does not require it.\n\nShipped exactly the design the deferred entry called for: src/lib/leads/pending-operation-announcement.ts, a plain pure function (pendingOperationAnnouncementText(isPending): string, returning a fixed 'Working…' message or empty string) with zero DOM/JSX, unit-tested in the normal node Vitest environment. Wired a single always-mounted `<div aria-live=\"assertive\" role=\"status\" className=\"sr-only\">{pendingOperationAnnouncementText(isPending)}</div>` at the very top of leads-client.tsx's returned JSX (before any conditionally-rendered panel), driven directly by the same shared `isPending` every one of the ~64 action buttons already disables on - no per-button, per-panel, or per-action-site changes needed, so it covers all ~64 buttons (plus the 3 that already had their own label ternary) uniformly and is immune to the focus-loss race since it depends only on isPending, never on which element currently has focus. Kept the region always in the DOM (never conditionally rendered) since aria-live only announces text CHANGES within a persistent element, not an element's own appearance.\n\nsrc/lib/leads/pending-operation-announcement.test.ts - 2 new Vitest cases (true -> message, false -> empty string). Dev-server smoke check: started `npm run dev`, confirmed OPERATOR_DASHBOARD_PASSWORD is unset so /dashboard/leads is directly reachable (per operator-auth-env-banner's own documented open-when-unset behavior), and curled the rendered HTML to confirm the region is present at rest with the exact expected markup (`<div aria-live=\"assertive\" role=\"status\" class=\"sr-only\"></div>`, empty text as pendingOperationAnnouncementText(false) requires) and the page still returns 200 with its normal content. Did not attempt a live-click interaction check: this repo has no Playwright/browser-automation npm dependency installed (confirmed via `npm ls playwright`), and installing one ad hoc for a single smoke check would itself be exactly the kind of new-dependency/new-test-convention structural decision the deferred entry explicitly called out-of-scope for a small fix - the static-render curl check plus the pure-function unit tests are the correct-scoped verification here, consistent with the new-capability carve-out.\n\nsrc/lib/leads/pending-operation-announcement.ts, .test.ts - new files. src/app/dashboard/leads/leads-client.tsx - the wiring (one import, one always-mounted div). src/lib/process/business-decisions.ts - this entry. src/lib/process/prompt_process.tsx - the accompanying ITERATIONS entry. No NEXT_STEPS change - all five gated items (stripe-price-objects, lead-ingestion, marketing-content-scheduling, commerce-payouts-stripe-connect, github-actions-runner-unavailable) remain operator/legal/infra-blocked, unchanged. Diff-gate anchor moves to 67d22fc8 (origin/main tip after sibling PRs #946/#947 merged mid-iteration).\n\nFile-size check per AGENT_PROTOCOL's re-archive note: both process-log files re-measured via wc -c after merging both sibling PRs in - both comfortably under the 262,144-byte trigger, no re-archive needed this round.\n\nVerified: npx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json (0 errors) + npm run lint (clean) + npx vitest run targeted (pending-operation-announcement.test.ts, 2/2 passed) then full suite (green, including both sibling PRs' own changes) + a full clean rebuild (rm -rf .next && npm run build, clean, same route split, no new warnings) + the dev-server smoke check described above.",
