      "It found, and I independently re-verified by reading every file in the chain, a direct residual gap left by the immediately prior fix: checkout-setup-fee-skip-on-upgrade only changed what POST /api/stripe/checkout actually charges server-side — checkout-form.tsx (the client component rendering the /checkout page) never learned about the waiver, so it kept computing setupTotal = bundle.setupPriceUsd + (commerceAddon ? COMMERCE_ADDON.setupPriceUsd : 0) unconditionally and displaying the full setup fee in 'Due today', even on the exact upgrade checkouts the server now discounts. Confirmed by reading checkout/page.tsx, prefill-slug.ts, and checkout-form.tsx directly: loadCheckoutPrefillLead (prefill-slug.ts) only ever fetched getLeadBySlug, never listOrdersByLeadSlug, so CheckoutPrefill had no way to know a prior order existed.\n\nThis is the mirror image of the bug the prior fix closed, and arguably just as bad for trust: a Growth customer following sendGrowthUpsellEmail's 'setup is already covered' link would land on this page and see 'Due today: $699' ($500 setup + $199/mo) — the email says no setup fee, the checkout page shows one anyway — then actually get charged only $199 at Stripe a click later. Either the customer abandons at the apparently-wrong price before ever discovering the real (correct, lower) one, or they're confused by a form that visibly contradicts both the email and what Stripe ultimately charges. Confirmed this is a genuinely fresh, previously-unaudited gap: the checkout-setup-fee-skip-on-upgrade entry's own file list is server-only (route.ts, route.test.ts, docs/architecture) and never mentions checkout-form.tsx or checkout/page.tsx.\n\nFixed by threading the exact same signal the server route already computes through to the client form: loadCheckoutPrefillLead (src/lib/checkout/prefill-slug.ts) now also calls listOrdersByLeadSlug whenever a CRM lead resolves (skipped when no lead resolves, since an unknown/organic slug has no prior orders to have paid a setup fee against) and returns a new hasExistingOrder field on CheckoutPrefillLeadResult (made optional, not required, specifically so the several unrelated checkout-page-access.test.ts mocks that construct their own CheckoutPrefillLeadResult-shaped literals for pure rate-limit-composition tests didn't need touching). checkout/page.tsx passes this through to CheckoutForm as a new hasExistingOrder prefill field. Extracted the 'Due today' total and subtitle logic that used to live inline in checkout-form.tsx into a new pure module, src/lib/checkout/due-today.ts (checkoutSetupFeeTotal / checkoutDueTodaySubtitle) — unit-tested in the normal node Vitest environment rather than needing this repo's still-absent jsdom/@testing-library/react render-test infra, the same new-capability-addition carve-out precedent leads-client-pending-announcement-shared-status-region established (this is a display-parity fix layered on top of an already-shipped server change, closer to a new-capability addition for the client than a behavioral regression with prior test coverage to preserve) — and wired it into CheckoutForm in place of the old inline calculation. The subtitle logic mirrors the exact semantics the server-side fix already established: the Commerce add-on's own setup fee is never waived (checkoutSetupFeeTotal only zeroes bundle.setupPriceUsd, never COMMERCE_ADDON.setupPriceUsd), and the degenerate waived+zero-recurring case (which route.ts's own 400 guard already rejects server-side) gets a truthful 'Nothing due today' subtitle rather than crashing or showing a stale number, even though no real entry point reaches it client-side either.\n\nsrc/lib/checkout/prefill-slug.ts - added listOrdersByLeadSlug to CheckoutPrefillLeadDeps (required, matching getLeadBySlug) and hasExistingOrder to CheckoutPrefillLeadResult (optional, for the reason above). src/lib/checkout/prefill-slug.test.ts - updated all 6 existing loadCheckoutPrefillLead cases for the new field/dep, plus 1 new case proving hasExistingOrder: true when a prior order exists and confirming listOrdersByLeadSlug is never called for a slug with no CRM lead. src/app/checkout/page.tsx - threads hasExistingOrder through to CheckoutPrefill. src/lib/checkout/due-today.ts, .test.ts - new pure module + 10 new Vitest cases (normal monthly/annual/one-time-only display, waived monthly/annual display never mentioning a setup fee, the degenerate waived+no-recurring case, and the Commerce-add-on-unaffected cases for checkoutSetupFeeTotal). src/app/checkout/checkout-form.tsx - added hasExistingOrder to the CheckoutPrefill interface, replaced the inline setupTotal calculation and 'Due today' subtitle JSX with calls into due-today.ts. src/app/docs/architecture/page.tsx - one new paragraph immediately after checkout-setup-fee-skip-on-upgrade's own paragraph. src/lib/process/business-decisions.ts - this entry. src/lib/process/prompt_process.tsx - the accompanying ITERATIONS entry. No NEXT_STEPS change - all five gated items (stripe-price-objects, lead-ingestion, marketing-content-scheduling, commerce-payouts-stripe-connect, github-actions-runner-unavailable) remain operator/legal/infra-blocked, unchanged. Diff-gate anchor moves to d9d6680f (origin/main tip, PR #950 merge).\n\nProved via the git-stash technique: stashed only the three pre-existing source files (prefill-slug.ts, checkout/page.tsx, checkout-form.tsx — the new due-today.ts/.test.ts files were left untracked/unstashed since they have no prior behavior to regress to), confirmed all 6 updated/new prefill-slug.test.ts assertions failed exactly as expected (missing hasExistingOrder field, listOrdersByLeadSlug never called), then restored and confirmed all 135 tests across src/lib/checkout + src/app/checkout pass.\n\nVerified end to end with a dev-server smoke check (UI touched): started npm run dev, confirmed the default /checkout?tier=complete (no prior order) renders 'Setup fee + first month' and a $699 total; seeded a lead + order directly into local.db's SQLite tables via a raw node:sqlite script (bypassing the server-only guard on @/lib/db, which cannot be imported outside the Next.js runtime), then confirmed /checkout?slug=...&tier=complete for that lead rendered 'First month only — setup already covered' and a $199 total — exactly the $500 setup-fee difference the fix is meant to produce. Cleaned up the seeded rows and stray gitignored local.db/local.db-shm/local.db-wal files after.\n\nFile-size check per AGENT_PROTOCOL's re-archive note: prompt_process.tsx measured 210,844 bytes and business-decisions.ts measured 233,616 bytes via wc -c before this entry - both comfortably under the 262,144-byte trigger, no re-archive needed this round.\n\nVerified: npx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json (0 errors) + npm run lint (clean) + npx vitest run targeted (src/lib/checkout + src/app/checkout, 135 passed, 16 files) then full suite (3945 passed, 232 files, +11 net new) + a full clean rebuild (rm -rf .next && npm run build, clean, same route split, no new warnings) + the dev-server smoke check described above.",
